/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  economics04_building_royalty_breakeven -- THE FOUR ECONOMIC EXTENSIONS OF
  THE PIF REPORTS (DEV.md 4c C195, items E4 and E5), in one small plant.

  THE PLANT is sprayDryer07_design's: one sized spray dryer (100 kg/h of a
  40 wt% sugar liquor dried by hot air) standing in the 17-room, two-floor
  oral-solid-dose block of system/layoutDict (the gate check_gmp_layout's
  clean probe).  THE ECONOMICS is new: the dryer is costed, and the
  `economics {}` block of system/postDict declares

      buildings               E4   the building cost, from the rooms' areas,
                                   priced per room GRADE
      breakEven               E5a  the operating break-even and the NPV one
      royalty                 E5b  a royalty inside a declared patent window
      workingCapitalMethods   E5c  the three working-capital methods side by
                                   side

  EVERY NUMBER IN THEM IS AN AUTHOR-SET TEACHING ASSUMPTION, not a datum: a
  price per m2, a royalty rate and a fraction of sales are exactly the
  quantities the engine refuses to ship, and each block says so in its own
  `source` / `reason`.  The product is sold at a round price and the plant is
  small, so the appraisal is a demonstration of the arithmetic, not a
  business case; read the run's own printed ladders against
  bin/curate/check_economic_extensions.py, which recomputes each figure from
  the case's declarations.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description   "Economic extensions: a building priced by room grade, the two break-evens, a royalty with a patent window, three working-capital methods";

verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    {}
    massBalance    {}
    energyBalance  {}
}
